  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 275, 'Welcome a roommate''s traditions into your shared home, like making space for their decorations or their quiet time.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 276, 'Pick out a song, scent or color that always meant celebration in your family, and bring it into an ordinary day.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 277, 'Pause for a moment of quiet before a shared meal, in whatever way fits your family''s beliefs.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 278, 'Mark the first day of a new season at work by sharing one seasonal photo or word with a colleague.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 279, 'Jot a few notes after a new tradition, what worked and what to change, so next time is easier.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 280, 'Tell a child about a friend''s tradition you have joined, so they grow up curious about others.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 281, 'Press a leaf or flower from an autumn walk, the way someone in your family once did.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 282, 'Greet each new month with a small household ritual, like turning the calendar page together and planning one simple outing.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 283, 'Pause at the halfway point of the year to notice what has grown in you since it began.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 284, 'Agree with friends on one day each season to meet outdoors, whatever the weather.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 285, 'Suggest to your library a story hour about traditions from many cultures, and offer to help.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 286, 'Draw a small emblem for your family or chosen family, using shapes or colors that matter in your heritage.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 287, 'Plan a weekly hour without screens on a set evening and fill it with conversation or games.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 288, 'Write a short end of year letter to a friend far away, sharing three moments you want them to know about.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 289, 'Suggest a yearly day out with a sibling, cousin or old friend, even just to a nearby town or park.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 290, 'Encourage a teenager to bring a friend to a family tradition, so it feels like theirs too.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 291, 'Carry on one small custom for someone who can no longer keep it, like sending their yearly greetings or watering their plants.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 292, 'Spend a few minutes with a pet each evening, brushing them or simply sitting close.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 293, 'If you are far from home this season, recreate one small piece of how home marks it, like a song or a scent.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 294, 'Create a ritual for starting something new, like a walk to a favorite spot and a written wish before a new job or term.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 295, 'Answer gently when someone asks about your tradition, even an awkward question, and help them understand.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 296, 'Tell a friend about a person who carried a tradition for your family, and what you admire about them.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 297, 'Bring a flower or a pretty leaf home for the table once a week.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 298, 'Put together a yearly memory box and add one small keepsake from this season.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 299, 'Try out a tradition you read about or saw in a film, just once, and see if it fits your home.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 300, 'Pass along an invitation to a public celebration to someone who might not hear about it otherwise.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 301, 'Play a recording of a relative''s voice, or a song they loved, and let yourself remember.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 302, 'Swap stories with a coworker on a short walk at the same time each week.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 303, 'Remember the day a pet joined your family with an extra long walk or a new photo together.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 304, 'Choose a tradition you once shared with someone now gone, and adapt it so you can do it alone or with others.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 305, 'Show a friend your favorite way to keep a tradition when money is tight, like a free version that still feels special.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 306, 'Discover the meaning of a symbol your family uses at celebrations, like a color, a flower or a shape.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 307, 'Set out the next morning''s cups or bowls each night, a small act of care for whoever wakes first.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 308, 'Go see a seasonal sight near you, like migrating birds, summer fireflies or a field of frost at dawn.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 309, 'Open a new tradition with a few words of welcome the first time you try it, so it feels like a beginning.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 310, 'Accept an invitation to someone else''s tradition with gratitude, and follow their lead.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 311, 'Recite a rhyme, verse or poem from your childhood and notice which words you still know.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 312, 'Start a little book of family quotes and add the funny things people say at home each week.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 313, 'Write the year''s best moments on small cards and read them aloud with someone at the end of the year.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 314, 'Swap roles in a family tradition, so the usual host gets to be a guest.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 315, 'Keep a tradition alive in a group that is shrinking, like a choir or club, by bringing one new person along.'),
