  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 317, 'Write the date and one line about the day on a wall calendar each evening.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 318, 'Open the box of things you bring out only once a year, like a special cloth or a game, slowly and with a little ceremony.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 319, 'Keep a running list on your phone of tradition ideas you hear about, and pick from it when you want something new.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 320, 'Contribute a few lines about a tradition to a school, club or community newsletter.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 321, 'Offer to help an older neighbor with something a tradition needs, like hanging decorations at ground level or writing cards.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 322, 'Sit on a doorstep or balcony for a few minutes after dinner and listen to the neighborhood settle.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 323, 'Fly a kite, ride a carousel or roll down a grassy slope once a year, for the child you once were.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 324, 'Make up the tradition you always wished you had as a child, and give it to yourself now in a small way.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 325, 'Bring an absent friend into a gathering by reading out a message they sent or sharing their photo.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 326, 'Notice a tradition from your heritage on a menu, in a shop window or at a street fair, and smile at the connection.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 327, 'Begin each morning with a short wish or hope for the day, said in words that fit your beliefs.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 328, 'Hold a small seasonal swap with friends for books, plants or clothes you no longer need.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 329, 'Teach your new tradition to a friend so it can live in more than one home.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 330, 'Give a young person a role in a family tradition, like reading the welcome or choosing the music.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 331, 'Create a simple family tree that lists one tradition next to each person''s name.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 332, 'Hold a weekly show and tell at dinner where each person brings one thing they found or made.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 333, 'Reread a favorite book that suits the season, and let it become your yearly reread.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 334, 'Let a new tradition be imperfect: if it goes wrong, laugh and try again next time.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 335, 'Ask a friend far from home which place nearby reminds them of home, and go there together.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 336, 'Start a shared online album where relatives far away can add photos of their traditions.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 337, 'Play one quick round of a word game over breakfast each morning, just for the laughs.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 338, 'Greet the turn of the year at a time that suits you, even if that means sleeping early and waking to a sunrise.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 339, 'Pair a new ritual with something you already do, like a moment of stillness after you lock the door at night.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 340, 'Talk with a teenager about which family traditions feel meaningful to them and which feel stale.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 341, 'Explore how a tradition from your faith or culture echoes one from another, and notice what they share.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 342, 'Name a ritual you already share with someone and tell them how much you love it.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 343, 'Ask a friend which yearly moment they look forward to most, and find a way to be part of it.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 344, 'Find a place that will be the home of a new tradition, like a corner of the park or a spot by the window.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 345, 'Gift a younger relative a homemade booklet of your family''s traditions and the stories behind them.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 346, 'Draw a family tradition as a short comic strip, from the first moment to the last.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 347, 'Offer a standing seat at one of your regular meals to a neighbor or friend who lives alone.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 348, 'Spend a winter afternoon making something with your hands, like a scarf, a drawing or a paper snowflake.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 349, 'Start a winter tradition of a living room camp out, with blankets, a flashlight and stories.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 350, 'Volunteer to take photos at a friend''s celebration, if they would like that, so they can stay in the moment.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 351, 'Mail a handwritten card for an occasion your family has always marked, to keep the habit going.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 352, 'Draw or doodle together for ten minutes on a set evening, with no goal but fun.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 353, 'Wear the season''s color for a day, like gold in autumn or green in spring, and see who notices.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 354, 'Picture your new tradition many years from now and imagine who might be keeping it then.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 355, 'Learn about a tradition of the original people of the land where you live, from a source they created.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 356, 'Note one tradition from your workplace or a club you belong to, and find out how it started.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 357, 'Save the last few minutes before sleep for the same small thing, like a page of a book or a few calm breaths.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 358, 'Leave something for the next season''s you, like a kind note in a coat pocket you will wear again.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 359, 'Gift someone a small kit for starting their own tradition, like cards with questions for their dinner table.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 360, 'Reach out to someone spending a special day alone, and invite them to share part of yours.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 361, 'Close the evening by writing down which tradition from your past you feel most grateful for.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 362, 'End this season of rituals by doing your favorite one slowly, with your full attention.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 363, 'End the year by thanking yourself for one thing you did this year that took courage.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 364, 'Look back at the traditions you started this season and pick the one you most want to carry on.'),
  ('keeping-traditions-alive', 365, 'Close a gathering by asking everyone which tradition they hope to keep sharing.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
